00:02:12,177 --> 00:02:14,737
I'm sorry!

1176
00:02:14,737 --> 00:02:15,847
H-Hey!

1177
00:02:15,947 --> 00:02:18,757
Oh, thank goodness! Are you hurt?

1178
00:02:18,757 --> 00:02:21,037
No, I'm fine.

1179
00:02:21,037 --> 00:02:23,317
I'm really, really sorry!

1180
00:02:23,317 --> 00:02:24,667
Don't worry about it.

1181
00:02:24,867 --> 00:02:26,997
What were you doing, anyway?

1182
00:02:26,997 --> 00:02:28,887
This tree was practically calling out to me.

1183
00:02:28,887 --> 00:02:30,787
I <i>had</i> to climb it.

1184
00:02:30,787 --> 00:02:33,537
But I got ahead of myself, and my foot slipped.

1185
00:02:33,537 --> 00:02:35,677
Wait, what about you? Are you hurt?

1186
00:02:35,807 --> 00:02:37,387
I'm fine.

1187
00:02:37,387 --> 00:02:39,687
You're so nice, Sasaki-san.

1188
00:02:39,817 --> 00:02:42,147
Huh? How do you know my name?

1189
00:02:42,277 --> 00:02:44,257
You're Sasaki Atsuko-san, right?

1190
00:02:44,257 --> 00:02:46,517
We're in the same class.

1191
00:02:46,517 --> 00:02:47,587
Oh...

1192
00:02:47,587 --> 00:02:51,667
I haven't learned the names 
or faces of anyone in our class yet.

1193
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:52,987
I'm sorry.

1194
00:02:52,987 --> 00:02:54,427
Really?

1195
00:02:54,427 --> 00:02:56,517
Then, I'll introduce myself now.

1196
00:02:56,517 --> 00:02:57,747
My name is—

1197
00:03:00,377 --> 00:03:03,927
<i>She gave me a new world.</i>

1198
00:03:04,757 --> 00:03:06,947
<i>Every day was exciting and fun.</i>

1199
00:03:07,377 --> 00:03:09,377
<i>The days I had spent reading books alone</i>

1200
00:03:09,377 --> 00:03:12,007
<i>and never talking to anyone</i>

1201
00:03:12,357 --> 00:03:13,867
<i>didn't seem real anymore.</i>

1202
00:03:15,437 --> 00:03:18,767
Acchan... I'm done for.

1203
00:03:18,767 --> 00:03:20,547
The rest is up to you.

1204
00:03:20,547 --> 00:03:22,277
What are you talking about?

1205
00:03:22,277 --> 00:03:24,857
It hasn't even been ten minutes yet.

1206
00:03:24,857 --> 00:03:27,347
You want to miss out on getting 
into high school this year?

1207
00:03:27,347 --> 00:03:29,567
But I'm just so sleepy...

1208
00:03:29,567 --> 00:03:35,077
This reference book must have a curse 
on it that makes people sleepy!

1209
00:03:36,367 --> 00:03:38,487
Okay, if you pass the exam,

1210
00:03:38,487 --> 00:03:42,027
I'll let you play my most 
prized otome game all you want.

1211
00:03:42,027 --> 00:03:44,767
Really?! Thanks, Acchan!

1212
00:03:44,767 --> 00:03:47,697
I'll pass the exam to get 
into high school, whatever it takes!

1213
00:03:48,047 --> 00:03:52,257
A

1214
00:03:48,047 --> 00:03:52,257
PASSING EXAMINEES

1215
00:03:53,777 --> 00:03:56,097
What now? Want to stop by my place?

1216
00:03:56,097 --> 00:03:57,687
I'm gonna head home for today.

1217
00:03:57,687 --> 00:04:01,377
I want to conquer the black-hearted, 
sadistic prince by tonight.

1218
00:04:01,377 --> 00:04:04,147
You've really gotten into Fortune Lover, huh?

1219
00:04:04,147 --> 00:04:05,617
Okay, good luck.

1220
00:04:05,617 --> 00:04:08,187
Thanks! See you tomorrow!

1221
00:04:13,317 --> 00:04:16,007
<i>I took for granted that those 
days would last forever...</i>

1222
00:04:18,377 --> 00:04:20,557
<i>but they ended so suddenly.</i>

1223
00:04:30,847 --> 00:04:34,507
<i>She was involved in a traffic 
accident on the way to school.</i>

1224
00:04:35,877 --> 00:04:38,887
<i>She'll never come back.</i>

1225
00:04:57,907 --> 00:05:01,407
A

1226
00:04:57,907 --> 00:05:01,407
A

1227
00:04:57,907 --> 00:05:01,407
A

1228
00:04:57,907 --> 00:05:01,407
A

1229
00:04:57,907 --> 00:05:01,407
Acchan, I can't conquer the

1230
00:04:57,907 --> 00:05:01,407
black-hearted, sadistic prince!

1231
00:05:05,587 --> 00:05:08,347
This was her last message to me?

1232
00:05:11,047 --> 00:05:13,457
A

1233
00:05:11,047 --> 00:05:13,457
A

1234
00:05:11,047 --> 00:05:13,457
A

1235
00:05:11,047 --> 00:05:13,457
A

1236
00:05:11,047 --> 00:05:13,457
Acchan, I can't conquer the

1237
00:05:11,047 --> 00:05:13,457
black-hearted, sadistic prince!

1238
00:05:21,207 --> 00:05:22,267
<i>From now on,</i>

1239
00:05:22,267 --> 00:05:25,437
<i>I'll have to live my life without her.</i>

1240
00:05:25,607 --> 00:05:29,787
<i>I'll carry on in the new world 
that she gave me.</i>

1241
00:05:30,217 --> 00:05:37,167
<i>So if I have a chance 
to be reborn when my life ends,</i>

1242
00:05:37,167 --> 00:05:41,807
<i>I want to be friends with her again.</i>

1243
00:05:52,837 --> 00:05:55,057
Why am I...

1244
00:05:56,227 --> 00:05:58,707
Heave-ho...

1245
00:05:58,867 --> 00:06:01,157
and here we go!

1246
00:06:01,157 --> 00:06:02,667
Catarina-sama!

1247
00:06:03,627 --> 00:06:06,177
Morning, Sophia. Is something wrong?

1248
00:06:07,207 --> 00:06:09,817
I had a very sad dream,

1249
00:06:09,817 --> 00:06:11,937
and suddenly, I wanted to see you.

1250
00:06:12,147 --> 00:06:13,037
A dream?

1251
00:06:13,037 --> 00:06:16,707
Yes. It was a very, very sad dream.

1252
00:06:16,707 --> 00:06:20,217
I don't remember what 
happened in it very clearly,

1253
00:06:20,217 --> 00:06:23,587
but I think it was something 
that happened long ago.

1254
00:06:23,587 --> 00:06:25,347
Long ago?

1255
00:06:25,347 --> 00:06:27,667
I don't mean when I was a child.

1256
00:06:27,667 --> 00:06:31,317
Much, much longer ago than that...

1257
00:06:32,267 --> 00:06:34,967
This all sounds very strange, doesn't it?

1258
00:06:35,087 --> 00:06:37,547
No, it doesn't.

1259
00:06:37,547 --> 00:06:41,097
Bad dreams happen sometimes 
when you're nervous.

1260
00:06:41,097 --> 00:06:42,547
Nervous?

1261
00:06:42,547 --> 00:06:44,967
We have exams starting today, right?

1262
00:06:44,967 --> 00:06:48,627
I'm sure you had a sad dream 
because you're nervous about that.

1263
00:06:48,627 --> 00:06:52,057
But don't worry! I'm just as nervous as you!

1264
00:06:52,297 --> 00:06:54,247
Let's both do our best on the exams!

1265
00:06:56,397 --> 00:06:57,327
Okay.

1266
00:06:58,047 --> 00:07:00,597
I hate exams!

1267
00:07:00,597 --> 00:07:02,657
I just want to play all the time!

1268
00:07:02,657 --> 00:07:05,587
How long are you going to act 
as if it's still summer vacation?

1269
00:07:05,587 --> 00:07:09,737
If we don't pass the exam, 
we won't advance to the next grade.

1270
00:07:09,737 --> 00:07:13,147
But whether or not we get to 
the next grade isn't what's important.

1271
00:07:13,147 --> 00:07:16,157
It's whether or not we get the doom ending!

1272
00:07:16,157 --> 00:07:20,467
Maria doesn't seem to be in love 
with anyone at the moment.

1273
00:07:20,737 --> 00:07:23,627
She didn't have any summer flings, either!

1274
00:07:23,627 --> 00:07:28,097
We should continue our observation 
of developments in Maria's love life.

1275
00:07:28,097 --> 00:07:30,757
But right now, we need to focus on the exam.

1276
00:07:30,757 --> 00:07:33,337
If we don't advance to the next grade...

1277
00:07:33,417 --> 00:07:34,977
Catarina!

1278
00:07:34,977 --> 00:07:38,177
<i>How could you fail to advance 
to the next grade?!</i>

1279
00:07:35,657 --> 00:07:39,727
We'll get the doom ending 
when our own mother kills us!

1280
00:07:39,947 --> 00:07:42,077
L-Let's focus on the exam.

1281
00:07:42,257 --> 00:07:43,947
No objections!

1282
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:49,777
Your practical exam will consist 
of exploring these ancient ruins.

1283
00:07:50,137 --> 00:07:54,007
Deep in these ruins, where it's said 
that a great mage once lived,

1284
00:07:54,007 --> 00:07:56,867
there is a stone inhabited by magical power.

1285
00:07:57,017 --> 00:08:00,327
The team that brings it 
back here will pass the exam.

1286
00:08:00,327 --> 00:08:02,667
It's a bit like a treasure hunt, isn't it?

1287
00:08:02,667 --> 00:08:04,347
Yeah. Sounds like fun!

1288
00:08:04,347 --> 00:08:07,297
Everyone, do not take this task lightly.

1289
00:08:07,807 --> 00:08:11,147
The ruins are as complex 
as a maze on the inside.

1290
00:08:11,147 --> 00:08:15,557
In addition, there are various 
traps set at every turn.

1291
00:08:15,557 --> 00:08:16,867
Traps?

1292
00:08:16,867 --> 00:08:22,787
I heard that the great mage set traps 
to protect his magic tools from thieves.

1293
00:08:22,787 --> 00:08:26,247
Those traps still deter invaders to this day.

1294
00:08:26,247 --> 00:08:28,947
And they're tossing students 
into a place like that?

1295
00:08:29,067 --> 00:08:32,837
These teachers and second-years 
are here to serve as aides in the exam,

1296
00:08:32,837 --> 00:08:35,547
but still, you must not get careless.

1297
00:08:35,947 --> 00:08:40,007
Demonstrate your command of your 
own magic and everything you've learned

1298
00:08:40,007 --> 00:08:42,677
to make your way 
into the depths of the ruins.

1299
00:08:42,677 --> 00:08:46,677
Now, each team may proceed 
to their chosen entrance.

1300
00:08:46,667 --> 00:08:47,347
Yes, sir.

1301
00:08:47,347 --> 00:08:50,137
You two are on the same 
team as Alan-sama, right?

1302
00:08:50,137 --> 00:08:50,977
Yes.

1303
00:08:50,977 --> 00:08:55,407
I'm sad that you and I will be 
separated, but I'll do my best!

1304
00:08:55,407 --> 00:08:58,157
I'm worried about you, for many reasons.

1305
00:08:58,157 --> 00:08:59,237
Be careful.

1306
00:08:59,237 --> 00:09:00,107
I will!

1307
00:09:00,247 --> 00:09:02,967
Let's do our best with our team, too.

1308
00:09:02,967 --> 00:09:03,797
Right!

1309
00:09:03,797 --> 00:09:05,137
Catarina...

1310
00:09:05,137 --> 00:09:08,387
Don't leave my side once we're 
inside the ruins, all right?

1311
00:09:08,387 --> 00:09:10,737
You can count on me to look after my sister.

1312
00:09:10,947 --> 00:09:14,347
You really do follow us everywhere, 
don't you, Keith?

1313
00:09:14,347 --> 00:09:17,727
It was the teachers who chose 
the teams, Geordo-sama.

1314
00:09:17,727 --> 00:09:19,747
You may follow us, but that's all.

1315
00:09:18,977 --> 00:09:20,167
Did you say something?

1316
00:09:19,747 --> 00:09:22,157
She hardly even has any magic.

1317
00:09:20,807 --> 00:09:23,827
Such jokes won't work with me.

1318
00:09:22,287 --> 00:09:25,347
Must be nice to have so many 
people around to help her out.

1319
00:09:25,347 --> 00:09:28,377
She even has princes helping her. It's not fair!

1320
00:09:28,957 --> 00:09:30,847
I see you're all together.

1321
00:09:30,847 --> 00:09:34,287
As you've heard, this exam is very dangerous.

1322
00:09:34,287 --> 00:09:35,557
Be careful.

1323
00:09:35,697 --> 00:09:37,057
And good luck.

1324
00:09:43,807 --> 00:09:46,957
It looks like the setting for a novel.

1325
00:09:46,957 --> 00:09:49,737
Yeah. It's so dark and spooky.

1326
00:09:49,737 --> 00:09:52,457
If you're scared, do you want me 
to hold your hand, Sister?

1327
00:09:52,747 --> 00:09:57,607
As her fiancé, it's my job to escort her, <i>Keith</i>.

1328
00:09:57,607 --> 00:10:01,907
As her family, it's my job to protect her, <i>Geordo-sama</i>.

1329
00:10:02,377 --> 00:10:03,287
Huh?

1330
00:10:03,637 --> 00:10:05,737
I wonder what this is...

1331
00:10:09,347 --> 00:10:10,827
What happened?!

1332
00:10:19,487 --> 00:10:20,657
Sister!

1333
00:10:20,657 --> 00:10:22,317
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

1334
00:10:22,317 --> 00:10:25,117
Try not to touch anything!

1335
00:10:35,717 --> 00:10:36,817
What's that?

1336
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:39,747
We won't be able to get past that ice.

1337
00:10:39,747 --> 00:10:41,787
But there's no other way.

1338
00:10:41,787 --> 00:10:44,037
We'll just have to break through it.

1339
00:10:44,307 --> 00:10:45,887
I see now.

1340
00:10:45,887 --> 00:10:49,587
This is a test to see 
whether or not we can get through.

1341
00:10:51,177 --> 00:10:54,737
Everyone, stay back. This will be dangerous.

1342
00:11:16,867 --> 00:11:19,407
That's amazing, Geordo-sama!

1343
00:11:20,217 --> 00:11:21,497
Look!

1344
00:11:22,727 --> 00:11:24,357
Let's hurry through it.

1345
00:11:24,357 --> 00:11:25,497
Right!

1346
00:11:30,827 --> 00:11:34,347
It's so dark... I hope 
Catarina-sama is doing all right.

1347
00:11:34,547 --> 00:11:37,057
She'll be fine. Geordo's with her.

1348
00:11:37,057 --> 00:11:39,167
That's exactly what I'm worried about.

1349
00:11:41,527 --> 00:11:44,307
Mary-sama, Alan-sama, what's that?

1350
00:11:45,627 --> 00:11:48,147
It's the stone inhabited by magical power!

1351
00:11:48,257 --> 00:11:49,887
This means we'll pass the exam, right?

1352
00:11:52,927 --> 00:11:53,867
Wait!

1353
00:11:55,687 --> 00:11:57,597
Don't tell me this is...

1354
00:11:57,597 --> 00:11:58,867
Run, both of you!

1355
00:12:15,887 --> 00:12:17,127
Are you all right?

1356
00:12:17,127 --> 00:12:18,377
Yes...

1357
00:12:18,377 --> 00:12:21,107
I can't believe I fell for that trap.

1358
00:12:21,107 --> 00:12:22,247
How careless of me.

1359
00:12:22,247 --> 00:12:26,497
Still, this exam is much more 
dangerous than I expected.

1360
00:12:31,147 --> 00:12:33,797
Which way should we go?

1361
00:12:33,797 --> 00:12:35,947
Oh, there's something written here.

1362
00:12:36,497 --> 00:12:39,107
It's an ancient script.

1363
00:12:39,537 --> 00:12:41,207
I can't read it at all!

1364
00:12:41,207 --> 00:12:44,497
We've been learning ancient script in class, Sister.

1365
00:12:44,497 --> 00:12:46,837
Some of the characters have faded, though.

1366
00:12:47,447 --> 00:12:49,897
"You who wander within the labyrinth,

1367
00:12:49,897 --> 00:12:54,297
if you go east..." 
I can't read the next part.

1368
00:12:54,297 --> 00:12:56,407
I know what it is!

1369
00:12:56,407 --> 00:12:58,557
"If you go east, 
you will only march in place.

1370
00:12:58,557 --> 00:13:01,417
If you go west, you will struggle 
to follow a strenuous path.

1371
00:13:01,417 --> 00:13:04,307
Only the adventurer may 
proceed beyond the light."

1372
00:13:04,477 --> 00:13:06,307
This is a verse from a poem.

1373
00:13:06,307 --> 00:13:09,127
I'm amazed you knew that, Sophia!

1374
00:13:09,127 --> 00:13:11,217
I read it once before.

1375
00:13:11,217 --> 00:13:12,817
What could it mean, though?

1376
00:13:12,947 --> 00:13:16,757
I guess it means we should go west, 
even if the path is strenuous.

1377
00:13:16,757 --> 00:13:18,037
I agree.

1378
00:13:18,037 --> 00:13:20,177
Going east may lead to a dead end.

1379
00:13:20,177 --> 00:13:21,977
Then we need to go that way!

1380
00:13:22,837 --> 00:13:25,967
You always start with the dead 
ends in a dungeon! It's a rule!

1381
00:13:25,967 --> 00:13:27,787
There could be treasure chests there!

1382
00:13:29,377 --> 00:13:31,537
What are you talking about, Sister?

1383
00:13:31,537 --> 00:13:32,927
Let's go.

1384
00:13:31,537 --> 00:13:32,927
Huh? Wait...

1385
00:13:36,127 --> 00:13:40,137
It's not a dead end, but we can't go any farther.

1386
00:13:40,137 --> 00:13:42,277
We just need to swim across!

1387
00:13:42,677 --> 00:13:44,097
Something's in there!

1388
00:13:44,247 --> 00:13:47,847
What do we do?!

1389
00:13:48,197 --> 00:13:50,357
Leave this one to me, Sister!

1390
00:14:05,397 --> 00:14:07,187
That was rather breathtaking.

1391
00:14:07,187 --> 00:14:09,177
Yes, incredible!

1392
00:14:09,177 --> 00:14:10,987
Thanks, Keith!

1393
00:14:10,987 --> 00:14:12,877
All right, let's go.

1394
00:14:17,347 --> 00:14:20,437
<i>I wish I could be useful to them, too...</i>

1395
00:14:22,007 --> 00:14:23,887
Everyone, look out!

1396
00:14:23,887 --> 00:14:24,107


1397
00:14:24,077 --> 00:14:24,137
Come forth, Earth Bump!

1398
00:14:24,127 --> 00:14:24,247
Come forth, Earth Bump!

1399
00:14:24,247 --> 00:14:24,337
Come forth, Earth Bump!

1400
00:14:24,337 --> 00:14:24,457
Come forth, Earth Bump!

1401
00:14:24,457 --> 00:14:24,727
Come forth, Earth Bump!

1402
00:14:24,727 --> 00:14:24,837
Come forth, Earth Bump!

1403
00:14:24,837 --> 00:14:25,977
Come forth, Earth Bump!

1404
00:14:25,977 --> 00:14:27,977


1405
00:14:29,727 --> 00:14:32,007
Now we can get past it with no problem.

1406
00:14:32,007 --> 00:14:34,357
Well done, Catarina-sama!

1407
00:14:34,357 --> 00:14:36,157
Yes, you've saved the day.

1408
00:14:36,157 --> 00:14:38,107
Great job, Sister.

1409
00:14:39,207 --> 00:14:41,447
I'm glad my Earth Bump came in handy!

1410
00:14:42,407 --> 00:14:43,237
Huh?

1411
00:14:48,177 --> 00:14:49,567
Geordo-sama!

1412
00:14:49,567 --> 00:14:50,837
Stay back, Sister!

1413
00:15:06,047 --> 00:15:08,307
Is everyone all right?

1414
00:15:09,207 --> 00:15:10,227
Catarina?

1415
00:15:10,587 --> 00:15:12,117
Sister, where are you?!

1416
00:15:13,967 --> 00:15:17,127
Ow...

1417
00:15:17,617 --> 00:15:19,277
Where am I?

1418
00:15:19,757 --> 00:15:21,357
What do I do now?

1419
00:15:21,357 --> 00:15:23,407
I got separated from the others!

1420
00:15:26,457 --> 00:15:28,327
Geordo-sama!

1421
00:15:28,707 --> 00:15:29,957
Keith!

1422
00:15:30,557 --> 00:15:32,677
Sophia!

1423
00:15:32,677 --> 00:15:34,787
Where are they?

1424
00:15:35,587 --> 00:15:38,057
I never expected her to get lost!

1425
00:15:38,057 --> 00:15:39,907
Who would've thought 
she'd trigger a doom flag

1426
00:15:39,907 --> 00:15:42,217
in a way that had nothing to do 
with the game's plot?!

1427
00:15:42,217 --> 00:15:44,407
Well, our only choice is to keep moving!

1428
00:15:44,407 --> 00:15:46,287
Let's keep looking for a way out!

1429
00:15:46,287 --> 00:15:49,837
We don't want to waste 
energy running around blindly.

1430
00:15:49,957 --> 00:15:52,187
Let's wait for help to arrive.

1431
00:15:52,187 --> 00:15:53,537
What are you doing?

1432
00:15:53,537 --> 00:15:55,737
Looking for food!

1433
00:15:55,737 --> 00:15:58,647
We'll last longer if we have food, right?

1434
00:15:58,767 --> 00:16:00,917
Oh! Found some!

1435
00:16:00,917 --> 00:16:01,657
Ugh!

1436
00:16:02,017 --> 00:16:04,727
I don't think it's 
a good idea to eat that...

1437
00:16:04,727 --> 00:16:06,347
Isn't there anything else?

1438
00:16:06,347 --> 00:16:08,787
Oh, I found more!

1439
00:16:11,877 --> 00:16:13,697
This'll hold me for a while.

1440
00:16:13,697 --> 00:16:16,027
There's no way I'm going to die here!

1441
00:16:23,127 --> 00:16:24,947
Is someone there?

1442
00:16:24,947 --> 00:16:26,567
Wait!

1443
00:16:29,887 --> 00:16:31,747
Brother!

1444
00:16:32,697 --> 00:16:34,947
Sophia? Did something happen?

1445
00:16:34,947 --> 00:16:37,347
We've lost Catarina-sama!

1446
00:16:38,387 --> 00:16:42,287
She disappeared while we 
were preoccupied with a trap.

1447
00:16:42,287 --> 00:16:45,147
Master Nicol, have you seen my sister?

1448
00:16:45,147 --> 00:16:47,577
No, she hasn't been this way.

1449
00:16:47,577 --> 00:16:49,737
What is it? Did something happen?

1450
00:16:49,737 --> 00:16:50,867
Everyone...

1451
00:16:51,877 --> 00:16:53,867
Catarina-sama is lost?!

1452
00:16:54,017 --> 00:16:56,867
Where could she have gone?

1453
00:16:56,867 --> 00:16:59,687
I hope she didn't get caught in a trap.

1454
00:17:01,597 --> 00:17:04,517
<i>That sad dream I had this morning...</i>

1455
00:17:04,517 --> 00:17:05,827
<i>Could it have been...</i>

1456
00:17:07,197 --> 00:17:09,367
You okay, Sophia?

1457
00:17:10,147 --> 00:17:14,467
I have a bad feeling. 
We have to find Catarina-sama!

1458
00:17:14,467 --> 00:17:15,947
A bad feeling?

1459
00:17:17,687 --> 00:17:19,727
Where are you?

1460
00:17:19,727 --> 00:17:22,307
Catarina-sama!

1461
00:17:25,617 --> 00:17:27,487
That's it! Her voice!

1462
00:17:28,497 --> 00:17:30,437
I'm going to pick up Catarina's voice.

1463
00:17:30,437 --> 00:17:33,027
Pick up her voice? How?

1464
00:17:33,707 --> 00:17:35,247
With wind magic?

1465
00:17:35,247 --> 00:17:36,197
Exactly.

1466
00:17:36,377 --> 00:17:39,637
I can pick up people's voices 
with my wind magic.

1467
00:17:40,067 --> 00:17:42,367
It should tell us which direction she's in.

1468
00:17:42,367 --> 00:17:43,867
Give it a try.

1469
00:17:43,867 --> 00:17:44,677
Right.

1470
00:17:56,297 --> 00:17:57,727
I'll help you!

1471
00:18:12,027 --> 00:18:14,047
That's weird.

1472
00:18:14,047 --> 00:18:17,407
I'm sure I heard footsteps.

1473
00:18:23,597 --> 00:18:25,577
I found more!

1474
00:18:26,037 --> 00:18:27,427
Mushrooms!

1475
00:18:29,767 --> 00:18:30,717
Mushrooms?

1476
00:18:31,047 --> 00:18:32,147
Mushrooms!

1477
00:18:32,147 --> 00:18:35,337
That was definitely Catarina-sama's voice!

1478
00:18:37,527 --> 00:18:39,477
What does "mushrooms" mean?

1479
00:18:39,607 --> 00:18:42,007
She didn't eat mushrooms, did she?

1480
00:18:42,547 --> 00:18:44,727
I'm just glad she's all right!

1481
00:18:45,187 --> 00:18:46,227
Let's go!

1482
00:18:49,377 --> 00:18:51,347
They're so hard to break loose.

1483
00:18:59,237 --> 00:19:02,747
This many should keep me alive 
for a good, long time!

1484
00:19:02,747 --> 00:19:06,637
I wish I had some soy sauce, 
but beggars can't be choosers.

1485
00:19:10,567 --> 00:19:12,197
Is someone there?

1486
00:19:23,707 --> 00:19:26,457
I refuse...

1487
00:19:26,457 --> 00:19:30,487
to meet my doom here!

1488
00:19:36,557 --> 00:19:37,927
Sophia!

1489
00:19:41,507 --> 00:19:43,167
Let go, Sophia!

1490
00:19:43,167 --> 00:19:45,407
No! I won't let go!

1491
00:19:45,407 --> 00:19:47,047
Never ever!

1492
00:19:47,047 --> 00:19:49,917
I don't ever want to lose you again!

1493
00:20:12,607 --> 00:20:14,217
Ouch...

1494
00:20:14,217 --> 00:20:15,897
Are you okay, Sophia?

1495
00:20:15,897 --> 00:20:18,627
Yes. What about you? Are you hurt?

1496
00:20:18,627 --> 00:20:20,547
I'm just fine!

1497
00:20:23,207 --> 00:20:24,437
Thank goodness!

1498
00:20:24,437 --> 00:20:29,287
Please don't ever leave 
again, Catarina-sama!

1499
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:33,167
Okay. I won't go anywhere.

1500
00:20:34,007 --> 00:20:37,237
Thank you for saving me, Sophia.

1501
00:20:37,767 --> 00:20:40,437
Was that whirlwind your magic?

1502
00:20:40,437 --> 00:20:42,887
No, it wasn't me.

1503
00:20:43,067 --> 00:20:45,987
Then... what was it?

1504
00:20:49,837 --> 00:20:50,907
Catarina!

1505
00:20:51,477 --> 00:20:52,447
Sister!

1506
00:20:52,957 --> 00:20:54,137
You're all right?

1507
00:20:54,137 --> 00:20:55,167
Yeah.

1508
00:20:55,167 --> 00:20:56,937
You all came to find me?

1509
00:20:56,937 --> 00:20:59,327
Thank goodness, Catarina-sama!

1510
00:20:59,327 --> 00:21:01,077
Sorry for worrying you.

1511
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:05,097
Hey, that stone...

1512
00:21:06,417 --> 00:21:08,467
It's the stone inhabited by magical power!

1513
00:21:08,467 --> 00:21:09,707
Th-This thing?

1514
00:21:09,707 --> 00:21:11,877
You did it, Catarina-sama!

1515
00:21:11,877 --> 00:21:13,807
Now we'll pass the exam!

1516
00:21:13,807 --> 00:21:16,167
Where did you find it?

1517
00:21:16,167 --> 00:21:18,847
Um, actually...

1518
00:21:21,107 --> 00:21:24,387
This many should keep me alive 
for a good, long time!

1519
00:21:24,597 --> 00:21:28,247
I was so hungry, I got 
absorbed in mushroom hunting,

1520
00:21:28,247 --> 00:21:32,667
so I didn't even realize it was 
the stone inhabited by magical power.

1521
00:21:35,077 --> 00:21:37,067
You never change, Sister.

1522
00:21:37,347 --> 00:21:41,817
Catarina remains strong and reliable, 
no matter the situation she's in.

1523
00:21:41,817 --> 00:21:42,677
